% ============================================================================
% spectral-classes.query.adj — a worked recall over the astronomy spectral-classes
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what color is a G star?":
% it states no astrophysics fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `spectral_class_color` rows and returns the color + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% color `red`, recall its spectral class — m). A letter that is not one of the
% seven main-sequence classes abstains honestly — the engine never invents a
% color.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli spectral-classes.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "spectral-classes.adj"

? spectral_class_color(o, $Color)      % expect blue    (hottest, bluest class)
? spectral_class_color(g, $Color)      % expect yellow  (our Sun's class)
? spectral_class_color(m, $Color)      % expect red     (coolest, reddest class)
? spectral_class_color($Class, red)    % reverse bind — expect m
? spectral_class_color(z, $Color)      % expect abstain — Z is not one of the seven main-sequence spectral classes
